---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, OPERATOR_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN, SITE_NAME } from '../../lib/legal';

const title = `Terms of Use | ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description =
    'Terms of Use for Canadian Credit Card Finder: informational comparisons only, not financial advice, verify card details with the issuer, and how affiliate links work.';
---

<LegalPage title={title} heading="Terms of Use" description={description} breadcrumb="Terms of Use">
    <p>
        These Terms of Use apply to your use of {SITE_NAME} at{' '}
        <a href="https://canadiancreditcardfinder.com/">{SITE_DOMAIN}</a> (the "site"), run by {OPERATOR_NAME}
        ("we", "us", "our") in Canada. By using the site, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please
        don't use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site is</h2>
    <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is a free, informational tool that helps people in Canada research and compare credit cards.
        We are not a bank, credit card issuer, lender, or broker. We don't take applications, make credit
        decisions, or have any say in whether you're approved.
    </p>

    <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
    <p>
        Everything on the site, including card details, rankings, "best of" lists, reviews, guides, and finder
        results, is general information only. It is not financial, legal, tax, or credit advice and doesn't take
        your personal situation into account. Think about your own needs, and consider talking to a qualified
        professional, before applying for any credit product.
    </p>

    <h2>Card information may change</h2>
    <p>
        We work to keep card information accurate and current, but issuers change fees, interest rates, rewards,
        welcome offers, and eligibility rules often, sometimes without notice. Information on the site may be
        out of date, incomplete, or contain errors.{' '}
        <strong>Always confirm the current terms directly with the card issuer before you apply.</strong>{' '}
        The issuer's terms and cardholder agreement are what actually apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links and advertising</h2>
    <p>
        The site shows ads served by Google AdSense, which help keep it free. Links to card issuers currently go
        directly to the issuer's site and are not affiliate links. We may add affiliate links in the future; if
        we do, we may earn a commission when you apply for or are approved for a product through one, at no extra
        cost to you, and we will disclose it on our <a href="/advertising-disclosure/">Advertising Disclosure</a>
        page. No issuer pays to be listed, ranked or reviewed. See our{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how ads and cookies work.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party websites</h2>
    <p>
        The site links to issuer and other third-party websites that we don't control. We aren't responsible for
        their content, offers, products, or privacy practices. Your dealings with any issuer, including card
        applications and cardholder agreements, are solely between you and that issuer.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Use the site for anything unlawful.</li>
        <li>Try to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the site or its systems.</li>
        <li>Scrape or copy large portions of the site's content or data for republication or commercial use without our permission.</li>
        <li>Interfere with the ads on the site, for example by generating fake clicks or impressions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
        The site's original content, design, and code are owned by us or used with permission. You're welcome to
        read, share links to, and quote short excerpts from the site with credit. Card names, issuer names,
        logos, and card images are trademarks of their respective owners and are used for identification only;
        their use doesn't imply endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>Google API Services</h2>
    <p>
        Separately from this website, {OPERATOR_NAME} operates an internal YouTube tool that uses YouTube API
        Services to manage the operator's own YouTube channel. By using YouTube features, you agree to be bound
        by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and the{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> applies. The tool
        is used only by the site operator, and no visitor data is accessed through it.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranties</h2>
    <p>
        The site is provided "as is" and "as available". To the fullest extent permitted by law, we make no
        promises or warranties that the site or its information will be accurate, complete, current,
        uninterrupted, or error-free.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of,
        or reliance on, the site or its information, including decisions about applying for, using, or
        cancelling a credit card. Nothing in these terms limits any rights you have under consumer protection
        laws that can't be waived.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that
        apply there.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these Terms of Use from time to time. When we do, we'll change the "Last updated" date at
        the top of this page. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email {OPERATOR_NAME} at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
</LegalPage>
